# MIRELLÉ INSPO — SYSTEM README
## Read this alongside MAIN_PROMPT.md and ALL_PLATFORM_LINKS.md before making any update.

---

## WHAT THIS SYSTEM IS

One aggregate content prompt covering **Pinterest, Facebook, Instagram,
X/Twitter, and YouTube** for Mirellé Inspo (nails/beauty editorial
brand, https://mirelleinspo.com). Jyotika runs it daily — she has zero
strategic/marketing/SEO background, so every decision is pre-locked
into the prompt. She only picks the order of the 4 non-Pinterest
platforms; nothing else.

**2 files run the whole system:**
1. `MAIN_PROMPT.md` — the full instruction set, all 5 platforms
2. `ALL_PLATFORM_LINKS.md` — every link pool, sectioned by platform,
   with rotation formulas

Both files are self-contained. A fresh agent with no other context
should be able to run either file correctly on its own.

---

## HOW TO REQUEST AN UPDATE (for Gaurav, next session)

Share both files plus a plain description of what's wrong or what you
want changed. Point to the specific platform/slot/field if you can —
"Facebook nail carousel isn't giving prompts" is more useful than
"Facebook is broken." Screenshots of actual bad output are the fastest
way to get an accurate fix, same as this session.

If something feels off in real output but you're not sure why, just
paste the output and ask — don't diagnose it yourself first.

---

## THE DAILY FLOW (how the prompt behaves)

1. Pinterest always runs first, fully automatically. No choice, no
   asking.
2. After Pinterest, the remaining 4 platforms (Facebook, Instagram, X,
   YouTube) are offered as a choice. Jyotika picks one.
3. That platform runs fully, delivers output.
4. Remaining platforms are offered again (list shrinks).
5. Repeats until all 5 are done. No stopping early — all 5 must be
   completed every day.

**Day 1 anchor for every rotation formula across every platform:
August 6, 2026.** `day_index = (today − Aug 6, 2026) in days`.

---

## PLATFORM-BY-PLATFORM SUMMARY

### Pinterest (runs first, always)
- 18 pins/day: 4 evergreen boards (Almond, Work Nails, Older Women,
  Nail Care Tips) + 1 seasonal board, fixed weekly format table
- Nail Care Tips uses the 256-link shared rotation (Links File Section
  1) — same link/topic as Instagram and YouTube that day
- Seasonal board rotates through full pools now (Links File Section 8),
  not fixed 3-link lists — only Back to School, Fall, Halloween are
  built out so far; other seasons will need their pools built when
  their window is about to open
- Every pin: Template (Infographic only) + Title + Description +
  Prompt + Link, each its own copy-paste box
- Inspiration Infographic overlay numbers = real researched stats
  ("50+", "44%"), never sequential ("1", "2", "3")

### Facebook
- 3 posts/day, 8+ hrs apart, via Meta Business Suite
- Daily pool: Nail image carousel (fixed count, rotates 3/4/5 by
  weekday) + Website article/link (evergreen 735 or seasonal 183 pool)
  + Infographic+BGM video (mobile 9:16 image, Gaurav adds music after)
- Slot order (AM/Midday/PM) rotates across the week, fixed table
- Nail carousel and Infographic both require **Prompt fields** (one
  per image) — this was missing originally, fixed this session
- Schedule: 8:00 AM / 1:00 PM / 8:00 PM

### Instagram
- 1 post/day, 5-slide informational carousel, 1:1 ratio only
- Same day_index/link as Pinterest and YouTube (Links File Section 1)
- Swipe arrow on slides 1-4 only — slide 5 has NO swipe arrow, just
  the down-arrow "Read full guide" CTA badge (fixed this session,
  was showing on all 5 slides including the last one)
- Caption must include the actual article link written out in full,
  directly after "Read full guide" — no separate "link in bio" line
  (fixed this session, link was missing from output)
- No hashtags, ever

### X / Twitter
- 4 posts/day, 2+ hrs apart, targets nail INDUSTRY professionals (not
  consumer traffic like other platforms)
- Only the Infographic slot carries a link — every other slot (Image
  carousel, Trend Report, Expanded, Roundup, Business/lead-gen) has NO
  link anywhere, no First Reply field exists in this system at all
  (major rebuild this session — First Reply was fully removed)
- Weekly Slot 3 rotation: Trend report (default) / Business (Wed, Sat)
  / Roundup (Fri)
- Business posts fold the CTA directly into post text — no separate
  CTA note field
- Roundup posts never say "below" or reference an attachment — X has
  no reply/thread structure in this system anymore, post text stands
  alone

### YouTube
- 3 Shorts/day, all Infographic+music, no exceptions (no filmed video,
  no carousel slot)
- Same day_index/link as Pinterest and Instagram
- **Does not count toward YPP/Shorts monetization** — that requires
  real filmed video, which this system doesn't produce. Channel runs
  for reach/branding only unless Gaurav revisits this later.
- 4 fields per Short: Prompt (mobile 9:16, text-heavy) + Title +
  Description (hashtags embedded) + Pinned Comment (fixed this
  session — Prompt field was missing originally)
- No tags field, no thumbnail field
- Schedule: 8:00 AM / 12:30 PM / 8:00 PM

---

## GLOBAL RULES (apply across all 5 platforms)

- **No em dashes ("—") anywhere in any written content, any platform,
  any field.** Added this session after being caught in Instagram
  output — use a period, comma, or rephrase instead.
- Every field goes in its own separate copy-paste code block — never
  combined into one paragraph.
- Genuine research required daily for every platform — never generic
  AI-sounding content. `site:mirelleinspo.com [slug]` first, open-web
  fallback if it doesn't index.
- Never invent a link — always pull from `ALL_PLATFORM_LINKS.md` using
  that platform's exact rotation formula.

---

## KNOWN OPEN ITEMS — NOT YET RESOLVED

1. **Pinterest seasonal pools beyond Back to School/Fall/Halloween**
   are not built. If the seasonal activation table triggers
   Thanksgiving, Christmas, New Year, Valentine's, St. Patrick's,
   Spring, Mother's Day, or Summer before their link pools are added
   to Links File Section 8, the prompt is instructed to stop and flag
   it rather than guess — this will need addressing before each of
   those windows opens.
2. **X's Trend Report vs Expanded Pool sub-rotation** is still loosely
   defined ("whichever pool fits today's research best") rather than a
   clean deterministic formula. Works, but isn't as precise as
   Pinterest's `mod` formulas.
3. **Facebook's seasonal activation window logic** references
   Pinterest's peak-date table as the reference pattern rather than
   having its own explicitly re-confirmed dates — functionally fine
   since they share the same seasonal concept, but worth flagging if
   Facebook and Pinterest ever need to diverge (e.g. different
   platforms emphasizing different seasons).
4. **One known duplicate link** in the Pinterest/Instagram/YouTube
   shared 256-link rotation (position 87 and 134 are the same URL) —
   confirmed with Gaurav to leave as-is, not a bug to fix.
5. **X scheduling tool** (Buffer/Metricool free tier vs X Pro paid) —
   noted as needing verification at time of use since free-tier
   availability was unconfirmed as of this build.

